      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:f2c5eb46eac2fdba",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did vēṇṭa mean, and what did pōruṁ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കാറ്റ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കാറ്റ് (kāṟṟŭ) — \"wind\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, matching Tamil kāṟṟu. The doubled റ്റ in the middle is one of the harder things Malayalam asks of a new mouth: a trilled ṟ held long, closer to a tt made further back than to anything English has."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In Kerala the word is bound up with the monsoon, and the wind that brings it off the Arabian Sea has its own name in the local calendar. A fisherman's day is decided by കാറ്റ് (kāṟṟŭ) before it is decided by anything else."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also does the work English gives to air, so a room with no കാറ്റ് (kāṟṟŭ) is a stuffy room rather than a still one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things the weather brings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kāṟṟŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kāṟṟŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pōruṁ, then kāṟṟŭ, and hold the doubled sound in the middle",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pōruṁ*, then *kāṟṟŭ*, and hold the doubled sound in the middle]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does കാറ്റ് (kāṟṟŭ) mean? (\"wind\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
