        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ചെളി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ചെളി (ceḷi) — \"mud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, and it names wet mud — the kind a monsoon makes, not the dry earth underneath it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kerala spends several months a year in it, and the word carries a mild disgust that the English one does not quite have. To say a thing has ചെളി (ceḷi) on it is to say somebody should deal with that."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ള at the end is the retroflex ḷ, tongue curled back again, and it is a different letter from the ൽ that closed the sand-word. Malayalam distinguishes three l sounds, and this run has now used two of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and the monsoon is doing the work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
