        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പുക",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പുക (puka) — \"smoke\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, matching Tamil pukai, and Malayalam has clipped the tail off where Tamil kept it — the same direction of travel you saw in the bone-word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A Kerala kitchen fire makes a great deal of പുക (puka), and the word covers steam and vapour as well, so a hot vessel and a smouldering one can be described with it alike."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is a short word doing a wide job, which is common in this layer of the language: the oldest words tend to be the briefest and the busiest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four, and this one rises."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
