        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കനൽ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കനൽ (kanal) — \"an ember, a live coal\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Inherited, matching Tamil kanal, and it names the live coal rather than the flame — what is left glowing when a Kerala kitchen fire has burned down, and what is banked at night to be woken in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is a distinction the language keeps carefully. The flame is one thing, the smoke you have just had is another, and the കനൽ (kanal) is the third: the part that holds the heat after the rest has gone."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The chillu ൽ closes it, the same bare l that closed the sand-word and the field-word before that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: the wind, the sand, the mud, the smoke, and the ember that outlasts the fire."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
